  "notes": "A formal word composed of {是|ぜ} (right/correct) and {認|にん} (acknowledge). Used in written language, official documents, and academic discourse. Implies deliberate judgment that something is acceptable or correct.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {是認|ぜにん}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to approve/endorse\n- {是認|ぜにん}⟦できない→できる：00557_dekiru⟧: unacceptable\n- ⟦{暗黙|あんもく}→暗黙：12876_anmoku⟧⟦の→の：09472_no⟧{是認|ぜにん}: tacit approval\n- {是認|ぜにん}⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{得|え}る→得る：02014_eru⟧: to obtain approval\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{承認|しょうにん}→承認：03237_shounin⟧: approval — more common, used for official permission\n- ⟦{認可|にんか}→認可：05879_ninka⟧: authorization — specifically granting a license or permit\n- ⟦{容認|ようにん}→容認：12344_younin⟧: tolerance/acceptance — accepting something even if not ideal",
